1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:01,743
A spinning wheel becomes

2
00:00:01,743 --> 00:00:03,710
a factory floor.

3
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:06,650
This is the Industrial Revolution.

4
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:08,964
Beginning in eighteenth century Britain,

5
00:00:08,964 --> 00:00:11,651
new textile machines shifted more production

6
00:00:11,651 --> 00:00:15,210
from family homes into large mills.

7
00:00:15,210 --> 00:00:17,700
Water powered early mills.

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,700
Later, burning coal produced steam

9
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:21,701
to drive machinery without relying

10
00:00:21,701 --> 00:00:23,840
on river currents.

11
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,794
Factories made goods faster,

12
00:00:25,794 --> 00:00:27,450
often more cheaply.

13
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:29,970
Railways and steamships connected factories

14
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:32,500
with distant markets.

15
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,890
Industrial towns grew

16
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:35,830
as people arrived for work.

17
00:00:35,830 --> 00:00:38,850
Many faced long, dangerous shifts.

18
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:40,650
Children worked too.

19
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:42,810
Coal smoke polluted the air.

20
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:44,576
Much raw cotton came from plantations

21
00:00:44,576 --> 00:00:47,430
using enslaved labour.

22
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:49,974
Industry spread across the world,

23
00:00:49,974 --> 00:00:52,658
reshaping how people made everyday goods,

24
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:54,300
earned a living, and travelled.
